 7 3268 1313","ad":"476 Kingsford Smith Drive"},{"n":"Coles Local","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":-27.433867,"lo":153.065532,"d":2509,"ad":"111-117 Racecourse Road"},{"n":"Second World War Hangar No. 7","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.4287,"lo":153.087,"d":1290,"ds":"Second World War Hangar No. 7 is a heritage-listed hangar at 116 Lamington Avenue, Eagle Farm, City of Brisbane, Queensland, Australia. It was designed by the United States Army and built from 1942 to c. 1952 by Manuel Richard Hornibrook.","wpu":"Second World War Hangar No. 7","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Second_World_War_Hangar_No._7.jpg/960px-Second_World_War_Hangar_No._7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Woolahra, Brisbane","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.4384,"lo":153.0633,"d":2640,"ds":"Woolahra is a heritage-listed villa at 1 Lexington Terrace, Hamilton, City of Brisbane, Queensland, Australia. It was built c. 1888. It was added to the Queensland Heritage Register on 21 October 1992.","wpu":"Woolahra, Brisbane","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Woolahra.jpg/960px-Woolahra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Windermere, Ascot","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.4346,"lo":153.0623,"d":2798,"ds":"Windermere is a heritage-listed villa at 14 Sutherland Avenue, Ascot, Queensland, Australia. It was built from c. 1886 to 1930s. It was added to the Queensland Heritage Register on 21 October 1992.","wpu":"Windermere, Ascot","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Windermere_%282007%29.jpg/960px-Windermere_%282007%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Chateau Nous","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.4327,"lo":153.0627,"d":2813,"ds":"Chateau Nous is a heritage-listed villa at 1 Rupert Terrace, Ascot, Queensland, Australia. It was designed by architect Douglas Roberts and built from c. 1937 to 1940s. It was added to the Queensland Heritage Register on 21 October 1992.","wpu":"Chateau Nous","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Chateau_Nous.jpg/960px-Chateau_Nous.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Cremorne, Hamilton","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.439,"lo":153.0595,"d":3011,"ds":"Cremorne is a heritage-listed villa at 34 Mullens Street, Hamilton, City of Brisbane, Queensland, Australia. It was designed by Eaton & Bates and built from 1905 to 1906. It was added to the Queensland Heritage Register on 21 October 1992.","wpu":"Cremorne, Hamilton","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Cremorne%2C_Hamilton.jpg/960px-Cremorne%2C_Hamilton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Glengariff, Hendra","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.42,"lo":153.0685,"d":3073,"ds":"Glengariff is a heritage-listed villa at 5 Derby Street, Hendra, City of Brisbane, Queensland, Australia. It was designed by Hubert George Octavius Thomas, with 1907 alterations by Robin Dods, and built from 1888 to 1889. It is also known as Dura and Glenaplin.","wpu":"Glengariff, Hendra","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Glengariff%2C_Hendra.jpg/960px-Glengariff%2C_Hendra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St John the Baptist Anglican Church, Bulimba","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.4517,"lo":153.0602,"d":3215,"ds":"St John the Baptist Anglican Church is a heritage-listed church at 171 Oxford Street, Bulimba, Brisbane, Queensland, Australia. It was designed by John Hingeston Buckeridge and built in 1888 by T Whitty. It was added to the Queensland Heritage Register on 9 July 2003.","wpu":"St John the Baptist Anglican Church, Bulimba","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/BulimbaAnglicanChurch.JPG/960px-BulimbaAnglicanChurch.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Pinkenba War Memorial","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.4235,"lo":153.1189,"d":3391,"ds":"Pinkenba War Memorial is a heritage-listed memorial at Eagle Farm Road, Pinkenba, City of Brisbane, Queensland, Australia. It was designed by Ernest Gunderson and built in 1919. It was added to the Queensland Heritage Register on 3 October 2005.","wpu":"Pinkenba War Memorial","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Pinkenba_War_Memorial_01.jpg/960px-Pinkenba_War_Memorial_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Greystaines","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.4389,"lo":153.0546,"d":3495,"ds":"Greystaines is a heritage-listed 8 bedroom, 6 bathroom, 3 kitchen house with 6 car garage (previously an apartment block) at 240 Kingsford Smith Drive, Hamilton, City of Brisbane, Queensland, Australia.","wpu":"Greystaines","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Greystaines.jpg/960px-Greystaines.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bulimba House","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.4461,"lo":153.0542,"d":3597,"ds":"Bulimba House is a heritage-listed detached house at 34 Kenbury Street, Bulimba, Queensland, Australia. It was designed and built by Andrew Petrie from 1849 to 1850. It is also known as Toogoolawah.","wpu":"Bulimba House","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Bulimba_House.jpg/960px-Bulimba_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"El Nido, Hamilton","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.4391,"lo":153.0524,"d":3711,"ds":"El Nido is a heritage-listed detached house at 194 Kingsford Smith Drive, Hamilton, City of Brisbane, Queensland, Australia. It was designed by Eric Percival Trewern and built from 1928 onwards by Burton Hollingsworth. It is also known as Cassa Anna.","wpu":"El Nido, Hamilton","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/be/El_Nido%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Anning Monument","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.4504,"lo":153.1259,"d":3726,"ds":"Anning Monument is a heritage-listed memorial at the corner of Hemmant and Tingalpa Road and Boonoo Street, Hemmant, City of Brisbane, Queensland, Australia. It was designed and built by William Busby in 1903. It is also known as Hemmant Boer War Memorial.","wpu":"Anning Monument","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Anning_Monument_front.jpg/960px-Anning_Monument_front.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ralahyne","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.4245,"lo":153.0564,"d":3737,"ds":"Ralahyne is a heritage-listed villa at 40 Enderley Road, Clayfield, City of Brisbane, Queensland, Australia. It was designed by George Henry Male Addison and built in 1888 and extended in 1904 to a design by Hall and Dods. It is also known as East View, Huntington, and Koojarewon.","wpu":"Ralahyne","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Ralahyne_%282009%29.jpg/960px-Ralahyne_%282009%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hemmant Christian Community Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-27.449,"lo":153.1265,"d":3738,"ds":"Hemmant Christian Community Church is a heritage-listed Union church at 69 Hemmant Road, Hemmant, City of Brisbane, Queensland, Australia. It was built from 1865 to 1866 as a Methodist church. It is also known as Hemmant Methodist Church, Hemmant Uniting Church, and Tingalpa Wesleyan Methodist Church.","wpu":"Hemmant Christian Community Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Hemmant_Christian_Community_Church.jpg/960px-Hemmant_Christian_Community_Church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Brisbane ( BRIZ-bən; Turrbal/Yagara: Meanjin) is the capital and most populous city of the Australian state of Queensland and the third-most populous city in Australia, with a population of about 2.8 million. Brisbane lies at the centre of South East Queensland, a bio-geographical and urban region with an estimated population of 4.1 million as of 2024. The central business district is situated within a peninsula of the Brisbane River approximately 15 kilometres (9 mi) from its mouth at Moreton Bay.","wpu":"Brisbane","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Brisbane_CBD_seen_from_Kangaroo_Point%2C_2024%2C_01_%282%29.jpg/960px-Brisbane_CBD_seen_from_Kangaroo_Point%2C_2024%2C_01_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}